taris-brcmfmac-dkms

The Broadcom FullMAC Wi-Fi driver (drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac, with the
headers of brcm80211/include) from Asahi Linux's kernel source
(https://github.com/AsahiLinux/linux), by Broadcom Corporation, its other authors and the Asahi
Linux contributors. Licensed under the ISC licence, as its files' SPDX lines say. The package
holds no kernel source: asahi-source.sh fetches the driver's source for each kernel it's built
for.

Changed by TarisOS (https://github.com/TarisOS/tarisOS) in 2026, in
0001-wifi-brcmfmac-pcie-BCM4378-L1-substates-only-while-the-firmware-runs.patch: the BCM4378's PCIe
link uses ASPM L1.1 and L1.2 while its firmware runs, and they're switched off before every chip
reset, so the firmware always starts with L1 alone, as at boot, and again when the machine wakes,
until 90 seconds after the wake.
pcie.c, the file it changes, says so near its top (taris-notices.patch). Both patches are in
TarisOS's source, packaging/pkgbuilds/taris-brcmfmac-dkms.
